From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Peter Kvitek <kvitekp@chromium.org>
Date: Mon, 26 Oct 2026 19:13:33 -0700
Subject: Printing: Guard deferred PrintWithParams against nested print

When `PrintRenderFrameHelper::PrintWithParams()` defers printing to load
lazy or print-media resources, the `OnPrintWithParamsFinished()`
continuation ran outside `ScopedIPC` and without `print_in_progress_`
set. This allowed page scripts (e.g. via `matchMedia('print')` or
`beforeprint`/`afterprint` listeners) to invoke `window.print()` and
initiate a nested `PrintPreview` or `ScriptedPrint` operation while
`PrintPages()` was on the stack, overwriting `print_pages_params_` or
destroying `PrintRenderFrameHelper`.

To fix this:
- Apply `ScopedIPC` and set `print_in_progress_ = true` for the duration
  of `OnPrintWithParamsFinished()`.
- Store `print_with_params_callback_` and block concurrent print
  entry points while `PrintWithParams()` is pending (and vice versa
  when `print_in_progress_` is set).
- Clone `print_pages_params_->params` instead of holding raw references
  across page rendering calls.

Bug: 574409275
Change-Id: I44a26836a6155f61aeb512b6d3adf07783ad4e4e
Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/chromium/src/+/8639474
Reviewed-by: Lei Zhang <thestig@chromium.org>
Commit-Queue: Peter Kvitek <kvitekp@chromium.org>
Cr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#1727629}

Electron adaptation notes (43-x-y):
On this branch PrintWithParams() still prints synchronously (no WillPrintSoon()/OnPrintWithParamsFinished() deferral) and there are no InitiatePrintAndroid()/FinishPrintAndroid(), so the OnPrintWithParamsFinished() and Android hunks were folded into / dropped from PrintWithParams(): it now fails early when a print is already in progress, stores the callback before dispatching beforeprint, sets print_in_progress_ around the synchronous print, and uses a WeakPtr across PrintPages()/FinishFramePrinting()/afterprint, exactly as the upstream deferred path does. All other guards and the PrintParams cloning applied unchanged. The chrome/browser devtools browser test did not merge and was dropped (test-only, not compiled by Electron).

